# nr-tui-termtext-width: wiring for the new crate mixdog-termtext (lead applies, then deletes this file)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml  [workspace] members
Anchor: the line `"crates/mixdog-js",` in `members` (the list is not alphabetical). Add directly after it the line
    "crates/mixdog-termtext",

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml  [workspace.dependencies]
Anchor: the line `mixdog-js = { path = "crates/mixdog-js" }`. Add, in alphabetical place:
    mixdog-termtext = { path = "crates/mixdog-termtext" }
(No new external crate: unicode-segmentation, serde_json and mixdog-js are already workspace dependencies; Cargo.lock gets one
new `[[package]] name = "mixdog-termtext"` with dependencies mixdog-js, unicode-segmentation, serde_json (dev).)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-termtext/Cargo.toml
After the workspace hack is regenerated, add to [dependencies] the line every peer crate has:
    mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }
and list mixdog-termtext in native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml if hakari does so for peers.
mixdog-fsio (named by the plan) is not a dependency: nothing in this task reads a file.

## 4. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no registration. The crate is a library; consumers (nr-tui-termtext-ansi-wrap and
later) add `mixdog-termtext = { workspace = true }` themselves.

## Interfaces added (for the tasks that consume them)
mixdog_termtext::{display_width, display_width_with, string_width, StringWidthOptions, strip_ansi},
policy::{display_width, display_width_with}, width::{string_width, StringWidthOptions}, strip::strip_ansi,
grapheme::{Grapheme, graphemes_with_widths, next_boundary, prev_boundary, utf16_to_byte, byte_to_utf16, utf16_len},
and the declared (unimplemented!) interfaces ansi/wrap/slice/truncate/spans named in the plan, for nr-tui-termtext-ansi-wrap.
